From stable+bounces-317760-greg=kroah.com@vger.kernel.org Tue Sep  8 14:34:51 2026
From: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Date: Tue,  8 Sep 2026 08:19:52 -0400
Subject: iomap: simplify iomap_dio_bio_iter
To: stable@vger.kernel.org
Cc: Christoph Hellwig <hch@lst.de>, Damien Le Moal <dlemoal@kernel.org>, "Darrick J. Wong" <djwong@kernel.org>, Anuj Gupta <anuj20.g@samsung.com>, Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>, Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Message-ID: <20260908121955.2049107-3-sashal@kernel.org>

From: Christoph Hellwig <hch@lst.de>

[ Upstream commit 6e7a6c80198ead08b11aa6cdc92e60a42fc5895f ]

Use iov_iter_count to check if we need to continue as that just reads
a field in the iov_iter, and only use bio_iov_vecs_to_alloc to calculate
the actual number of vectors to allocate for the bio.

Signed-off-by: Christoph Hellwig <hch@lst.de>
Reviewed-by: Damien Le Moal <dlemoal@kernel.org>
Reviewed-by: Darrick J. Wong <djwong@kernel.org>
Tested-by: Anuj Gupta <anuj20.g@samsung.com>
Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Stable-dep-of: 14b007e17881 ("block: validate user space vectors during extraction")
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
---
 fs/iomap/direct-io.c |   13 ++++++-------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

--- a/fs/iomap/direct-io.c
+++ b/fs/iomap/direct-io.c
@@ -344,7 +344,7 @@ static int iomap_dio_bio_iter(struct iom
 	blk_opf_t bio_opf = REQ_SYNC | REQ_IDLE;
 	struct bio *bio;
 	bool need_zeroout = false;
-	int nr_pages, ret = 0;
+	int ret = 0;
 	u64 copied = 0;
 	size_t orig_count;
 
@@ -426,7 +426,6 @@ static int iomap_dio_bio_iter(struct iom
 			goto out;
 	}
 
-	nr_pages = bio_iov_vecs_to_alloc(dio->submit.iter, BIO_MAX_VECS);
 	do {
 		size_t n;
 
@@ -439,7 +438,9 @@ static int iomap_dio_bio_iter(struct iom
 			goto out;
 		}
 
-		bio = iomap_dio_alloc_bio(iter, dio, nr_pages, bio_opf);
+		bio = iomap_dio_alloc_bio(iter, dio,
+				bio_iov_vecs_to_alloc(dio->submit.iter,
+						BIO_MAX_VECS), bio_opf);
 		fscrypt_set_bio_crypt_ctx(bio, inode, pos >> inode->i_blkbits,
 					  GFP_KERNEL);
 		bio->bi_iter.bi_sector = iomap_sector(iomap, pos);
@@ -481,16 +482,14 @@ static int iomap_dio_bio_iter(struct iom
 		dio->size += n;
 		copied += n;
 
-		nr_pages = bio_iov_vecs_to_alloc(dio->submit.iter,
-						 BIO_MAX_VECS);
 		/*
 		 * We can only poll for single bio I/Os.
 		 */
-		if (nr_pages)
+		if (iov_iter_count(dio->submit.iter))
 			dio->iocb->ki_flags &= ~IOCB_HIPRI;
 		iomap_dio_submit_bio(iter, dio, bio, pos);
 		pos += n;
-	} while (nr_pages);
+	} while (iov_iter_count(dio->submit.iter));
 
 	/*
 	 * We need to zeroout the tail of a sub-block write if the extent type
